        "procedure": "Under N2, diphenyldipyrrolylmethane (1.0 g, 3.4 mmol) was added to a stirred suspension of KH (0.25 g, 6.7 mmol) in THF (100 mL). After a vigorous reaction, YbI2(THF)2 (1.92 g, 3.36 mmol) was added to the resulting clear solution, which immediately turned dark red. After stirring overnight, the mixture was centrifuged to remove a small amount of greenish material, concentrated to 20 mL, and layered with hexane (20 mL). Dark red diamagnetic crystals of 1 separated after standing at room temperature for 4 days (0.62 g, 0.16 mmol, 38%).",
